  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig 6, 'WHO SMART Guidelines approach'. A top band of five knowledge layers, each fed from a research and evidence base: L1 narrative (enhanced guidelines), L2 operational (digital adaptation kits), L3 machine-readable (machine-readable recommendations), L4 executable (reference software) and L5 dynamic (precision health models). A localisation bar leads down to five matching country adaptations: national policies and procedures, localized requirements, localized machine-readable code and standards, localized digital services, and dynamic applications trained for local outcomes. These feed data, evidence and impact, and an 'Evidence from digital implementations' arrow returns to the research base. Source: adapted from WHO SMART Guidelines.",
